      "message": "Thanks for updating the validation comment in PS 12! Stepping back and looking at this CL together with the rest of the relation chain, I found it quite hard to follow the distinction between \"raw\", \"real\", \"image-only\", \"frame\", and the multiple meanings of \"offset\" across `populate_cache()` and `get_frame()`.\n\n### Why the current terminology is hard to follow\n1. **\"Raw\" vs. \"Real\" vs. \"Image-only\" vs. `skip_image_offset()`**:\n   - We currently use 4 different pairs of terms for the same two concepts (`RAW_IMAGE_PROPS` vs `REAL_IMAGE_PROPS`, `!skip_image_offset()` vs `skip_image_offset()`, `\"raw capture modes\"` vs `\"image-only captures\"`).\n   - `skip_image_offset(type)` is especially confusing because it returns `true` when we **do** add the offset (skipping past the vendor header) and `false` when we **don\u0027t** add the offset. In `get_frame()`, `skip_image_offset(type) ? frame_params-\u003eoffset : 0` reads like a contradiction (\"if skip offset, use offset, else 0\").\n2. **\"Frame\" and \"Offset\" are overloaded**:\n   - In `get_frame()` and `FpImageFrameParamsCache`, `offset` refers to three different things:\n     1. The byte offset where the 2D pixel array starts inside `fp_buffer` (i.e. the size of the vendor header, e.g., 400 bytes on FPC1025).\n     2. The start of the capture type\u0027s output inside `fp_buffer` (`0` for vendor-format captures, or the pixel data offset for pixel-only captures).\n     3. The host\u0027s chunk read offset within the capture output (`FP_FRAME_GET_OFFSET(p-\u003eoffset)`), plus the final byte index in `fp_buffer`.\n\n### Proposal: Name each concept after its physical layer\nCould we add a couple of precursor CLs (and update this stack) to standardize on unambiguous names across these three layers?\n\n```text\nLayer 1: Physical Sensor Buffer (fp_buffer, size \u003d sizeof(fp_buffer))\n+------------------------+-------------------------------+------------------------+\n| Vendor Header (400 B)  | Pixel Data (160x160 \u003d 25600 B)| Vendor Footer (260 B)  |\n+------------------------+-------------------------------+------------------------+\n^                        ^                               ^                        ^\n0                        pixel_data_offset_bytes (400)   26000                    26260\n\nLayer 2: Capture Output Slice in fp_buffer (depends on fp_capture_type)\n  • Vendor-format captures (VENDOR_FORMAT, QUALITY_TEST):\n    |\u003c-------------------------- capture_size_bytes (26260) ---------------------\u003e|\n    capture_offset_in_buf \u003d 0\n\n  • Pixel-only captures (SIMPLE_IMAGE, PATTERN0, PATTERN1, RESET_TEST, ...):\n                         |\u003c----- capture_size_bytes ----\u003e|\n                         capture_offset_in_buf \u003d pixel_data_offset_bytes (400)\n\nLayer 3: Host Chunk Read Request (single EC_CMD_FP_FRAME call)\n                         |\u003c-- request_offset --\u003e|\u003c- request_size -\u003e|\n|\u003c------------- read_offset_in_buf ------------\u003e|\n```\n\nSpecifically:\n1. **Precursor CL 1 (`fpsensor_utils`)**: Replace `skip_image_offset(enum fp_capture_type)` with `is_vendor_format_capture(enum fp_capture_type)`:\n   ```cpp\n   bool is_vendor_format_capture(enum fp_capture_type capture_type)\n   {\n   \treturn capture_type \u003d\u003d FP_CAPTURE_VENDOR_FORMAT ||\n   \t       capture_type \u003d\u003d FP_CAPTURE_QUALITY_TEST;\n   }\n   ```\n   (And include the ASCII diagram above in the doc comment in `fpsensor_utils.h`.)\n2. **Precursor CL 2 (Devicetree macros + fix 3 DTS files)**:\n   - Rename `FINGERPRINT_SENSOR_REAL_IMAGE_SIZE` -\u003e `FINGERPRINT_SENSOR_PIXEL_DATA_SIZE`, `*_RAW_IMAGE_PROPS` -\u003e `*_VENDOR_FORMAT_PROPS`, and `*_REAL_IMAGE_PROPS` -\u003e `*_PIXEL_DATA_PROPS`.\n   - **Bug fix needed in 3 DTS files**: While checking why `offset + size \u003c\u003d max_image_buffer_bytes` wasn\u0027t universally true for pixel-only captures, I noticed that `zephyr/program/fpmcu/em32f967/niedzica.dts`, `zephyr/program/fpmcu/em32f967/nysa.dts`, and `zephyr/test/fingerprint/drivers/egis660/boards/native_sim.overlay` use a single `*_COMMON_IMAGE_PROPS` with the full vendor buffer size (`12800` / `15600` / `9980`) and a non-zero `image-data-offset-bytes` (`6400` / `7800` / `172`) for **all** capture types (including `SIMPLE_IMAGE`, `PATTERN0`, etc.). Once `get_frame()` uses the cached offset in `crrev.com/c/8495692`, reading `SIMPLE_IMAGE` on those boards will fail with `EC_RES_INVAL` because `6400 + 12800 \u003e 12800`. Splitting those into `*_VENDOR_FORMAT_PROPS` and `*_PIXEL_DATA_PROPS` (like `bloonchipper.dts`, `srebrna.dts`, and `smolec.dts`) fixes that bug!\n3. **In this CL (`8372808`) and the follow-up stack**:\n   - Name the cached offset getter/field `get_pixel_data_offset()` / `pixel_data_offset_bytes` (and in `crrev.com/c/8499507`, `struct FrameParams { uint32_t capture_size_bytes; uint32_t pixel_data_offset_bytes; }`).\n   - With the 3 DTS files fixed, `populate_cache()` (and `validate()` in `crrev.com/c/8499506`) can validate the exact invariant for both capture categories using `is_vendor_format_capture(capture_type)`:\n     - If `is_vendor_format_capture(capture_type)`: `capture_size_bytes \u003e 0 \u0026\u0026 capture_size_bytes \u003c\u003d max_image_buffer_bytes \u0026\u0026 pixel_data_offset_bytes \u003c capture_size_bytes`\n     - Else (pixel-only capture): `validate_fp_buffer_offset(max_image_buffer_bytes, pixel_data_offset_bytes, capture_size_bytes) \u003d\u003d EC_SUCCESS`\n   - In `get_frame()` (`crrev.com/c/8495692`), use `request_offset`, `request_size`, `capture_offset_in_buf`, and `read_offset_in_buf`:\n     ```cpp\n     uint32_t capture_offset_in_buf \u003d\n     \tis_vendor_format_capture(type) ?\n     \t\t0 :\n     \t\tframe_params-\u003epixel_data_offset_bytes;\n\n     uint32_t read_offset_in_buf;\n     if (check_add_overflow(capture_offset_in_buf, request_offset,\n     \t\t       \u0026read_offset_in_buf)) {\n     \treturn EC_RES_INVAL;\n     }\n     ```",
